    "# Run 9 — baseline subtraction, normalization, speciation (Fe Kα / Kβ)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Reads the already-processed XSpect results from disk — nothing is re-run\n",
    "through the pipeline.** Source file: `results/runs_9_static_xes.h5`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Post-XSpect analysis windows (all speciation restricted to these):\n",
    "\n",
    "| Line | Window (eV) |\n",
    "|------|-------------|\n",
    "| Fe Kα | 6380 – 6410 |\n",
    "| Fe Kβ | 7031 – 7075 |\n",
    "\n",
    "Processing order per line:\n",
    "1. **Crop** to the analysis window.\n",
    "2. **Baseline subtraction** — DISABLED for now (the polynomial fit was\n",
    "   over-subtracting into the peaks). The spectra pass through unchanged; the\n",
    "   cell is left in place as a stub so it can be re-enabled later.\n",
    "3. **Normalization** — area-normalize the spectrum.\n",
    "4. **Speciation** — peak metrics (centroid, FWHM, integrated intensity) and,\n",
    "   when reference spectra are available, IAD / LCF against them.\n",
    "\n",
    "> Run 9 uses a different von Hamos ROI/geometry than the Fe-foil runs, so its\n",
    "> energy axis differs from earlier runs. This notebook analyses run 9 in\n",
    "> isolation on its own axis."
   ]
  },
